  "theorem_contract": {
    "exact_cfi_vertex_and_degree_invariants": "For every connected 3-regular base graph G on V vertices, the CFI parity graph has N_CFI = 7 |V| vertices, E_CFI = 12 |V| edges, and maximum vertex degree Delta_CFI = 4 identically.",
    "luks_classical_polynomial_subsumption": "By Luks' theorem (JCSS 1982), Graph Isomorphism for graphs of bounded valence Delta <= 4 reduces to finding stabilizers in permutation groups with prime composition factors {2, 3} (solvable groups), solvable in deterministic polynomial time T_Luks = O(N_CFI^4) without quantum assistance.",
    "single_copy_quantum_fourier_extinction": "Single-copy quantum measurements on non-abelian coset states yield mutual information I(tau : K) <= 2^{-Omega(N log N)} bits, providing zero algorithmic utility.",
    "multi_copy_commutant_intractability": "Multi-copy collective measurements require diagonalizing commutants of dimension (N_CFI!)^k = 2^{Omega(k N log N)}, creating an exponential quantum bottleneck that exceeds Luks' O(N^4) classical runtime by an astronomical margin.",
    "universal_cfi_trilemma": "Every CFI gadget instance falls into: (I) gadget-promised parity decodable in O(|E|) time, (II) bounded-valence unpromised classically decodable in O(N^4) time by Luks (1982), or (III) computationally intractable quantum collective measurements."
  },
