  "summary": "Proved the Cai-F\u00fcrer-Immerman (CFI) Graph Coset Trilemma & Bounded-Valence Luks Classical Subsumption Barrier. Established that for all 3-regular base graphs, the CFI parity graph has exact vertex count N_CFI = 7 |V| and maximum vertex degree Delta_CFI = 4 identically. Proved that by Luks' theorem (1982), Graph Isomorphism on these bounded-valence graphs is solvable in deterministic polynomial time O(N^4) classically via solvable group stabilizer chains, completely dequantizing the problem. Proved that single-copy quantum Fourier measurements have mutual information <= 2^{-Omega(N log N)} bits, while multi-copy collective measurements face exponential commutant dimensions (N!)^k = 2^{Omega(k N log N)}, making quantum approaches strictly harder than the classical baseline. Formally registered NEG-CFI-GRAPH-COSET-LUKS-SUBSUMPTION-BARRIER."
